      "widgets_values": [
        "## Enlarge Small Images — VOSR 2.0 Upscale (2BZ)\n\n**Put an image in ① and run.** No prompt. Output is saved at **input size × scale**.\n(To keep the size and just add skin texture → use `2BZ_VOSR2_Retouch_AnySize`.)\n\n### Knobs\n- **③ `upscale`** = scale factor. Default 4. 2 · 3 · 4 recommended — the model was trained up to 16x but **quality isn't guaranteed above 4x** (per the node docs).\n- Output size guide: 512px ×4 = 2048px · 1MP ×2 = 4MP · 1MP ×4 = 16MP. For images already 2MP+, 2x is enough.\n- **Keep `tile_size` at 512** — the model was trained on 512px, so tiling is required once output exceeds 512px.\n- **VRAM**: `vae_tile_size` 512 default (~5.3GB measured for VOSR2). 1024 uses ~8.3GB at about the same speed.\n- `color_alignment` wavelet = match original colors (recommended).\n\n### Character\nVOSR 2.0 **preserves the original structure** instead of inventing new content (trained on images only, not a repurposed text-to-image model). Faces and text don't change, but it won't conjure lavish detail from tiny images with almost no information.\n\n### Requirements\n- **VOSR 2.0** node (search `VOSR` in ComfyUI Manager → comfyui-vosr2)\n- The ~7GB model auto-downloads on first run to `models/vosr2/VOSR2/`. Manual download: [CSWRY/VOSR](https://huggingface.co/CSWRY/VOSR/tree/main)\n- License: VOSR 2.0 code & weights Apache 2.0 (PolyU · OPPO, CVPR 2026)\n\n### Measured (RTX 3090 · 2026-10-14)\n| Input → Output | Time |\n|---|---|\n| 528×704 → ×2 (1056×1408) | 22s (incl. model loading) |\n| 264×352 → ×4 (1056×1408) | 6s (model already loaded) |\n| 360×360 → ×4 (1440×1440) | 11s |\n\nPeak VRAM about 6.4–6.8GB (incl. 2GB idle). Against ground-truth originals, ×4 clearly keeps wrinkles and beard better than plain resizing (sharpness 0.31→0.56, face similarity 0.946→0.957). At ×2 the difference is small.\n"
      ],
      "title": "⓪ Read me first"
    }
